        "date": "2026-11-07T23:11:41Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim): the rotary sweep states and can enforce its flute-rotation bound\n\nThe rotary chord pre-pass stands each sub-chord's tool on the mid pose,\nso a tool point w from the reference is off its true-pose place by up to\nw*2*sin(half/2). RotaryChordStats::flute_shift now states that bound\n(L = farthest field-bounds corner from the tip, capped at shank + r);\nwith center_sag it is a two-sided Hausdorff bound on the chorded sweep.\nStock::simulate_rotary_bounded / ChordLaw::flute_tol also enforce it\n(more sub-chords, refused by name past MAX_SUBCHORDS); simulate_rotary\nkeeps its count and output.\n\nAgreement suite stock_rotary_flute: field vs a brute-force sampled\nreference (4,001 poses of the controller's lerp), 0 sign misses past\nthe stated bound and past an enforced 0.05 mm; the sag class alone\nmisses by 9.5e-3, so the bound is the one covering the flute.\n\nFixes #20\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
